; interiors.xon -- the kettle set: the places behind doors.
;
; (interior NAME . PROPS): on a screen its (depth LO HI) covers, a door
; to it at its (chance PERCENT), the first of these to come up, one door
; a screen.  Its level is made by its own forms before the set's, with
; a way out and no way further down; (enter "TEXT") is said the first
; time in.  The band's caches are laid inside as they are out of doors.
; One that is (region SET) has no level of its own: its door goes
; into the region SET of this world.

(interior "farmhouse cellar" (depth 1 2) (chance 40)
  (enter "Stone steps down into the dark, and something shifting among the barrels.")
  (level-style rooms) (rooms 1 3) (room-size 4 10 6 10)
  (creatures 1 2) (items 1 2))

(interior "shepherd's bothy" (depth 3 3) (chance 35)
  (enter "Peat smoke and a cold hearth; whoever lived here left in a hurry.")
  (level-style rooms) (rooms 1 2) (room-size 5 12 6 12)
  (creatures 1 2) (items 1 3))

(interior "old city vault" (depth 4 5) (chance 50)
  (enter "The Guild's lamps have been here before you, and the vault runs on past where they dug.")
  (level-style works)
  (creatures 2 4) (items 2 3))

; The town, on the hub: (region SET) makes its door the way into the
; region SET of this world, Kettle's five districts (see data/town),
; in place of a place of its own; a step off the town's edge comes back
; out onto it.  The game starts through it (see game.xon).
(interior "Kettle" (depth 0 0) (chance 100) (region "town")
  (enter "The road in past the watch house, and the setts underfoot."))
